![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

When sending `dspark_aux_hidden_states` over PP proxy tensors, we should flatten them to 2D (similar to `hidden_states.flatten(1)`) if they are 3D. This ensures consistency across PP ranks and prevents shape mismatches when they are written to the 2D `DSparkHiddenRowPool` on non-last PP ranks.

```suggestion
            proxy_tensors = {"hidden_states": hidden_states.flatten(1)}
            if capture_dspark:
                for idx, aux_hidden in enumerate(dspark_aux_hidden_states):
                    proxy_tensors[f"dspark_aux_hidden_states_{idx}"] = (
                        aux_hidden.flatten(1) if aux_hidden.ndim == 3 else aux_hidden
                    )
            return PPProxyTensors(proxy_tensors)
```

